From 4076c6f521eadccc05c1179c9a73baf004a0a7af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: drowzeys <drowzeys@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 15:18:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(tui): add a context-meter status line item
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The status line can already show remaining context headroom as a bare
percentage (context-remaining), but a numeric readout is easy to miss
while working. Add an opt-in context-meter item that renders the same
remaining-headroom value as a compact gauge, e.g.
'Context ▕██████░░▏ 77% left', so the line drains and recolors as the
Session approaches its context window.

- New canonical item 'context-meter' with 'context-bar' and
  'context-gauge' aliases; not part of the default item order.
- Renderer shares the runtime usage snapshot, model fallback, and
  error/warning thresholds with 'context-remaining', and shrinks to a
  shorter gauge before collapsing to the 'Ctx N%' minimal variant.
- Settings picker gains English/Chinese descriptions; the shared status
  line documentation covers the item, aliases, and opt-in semantics.

Validation: tsc -p tsconfig.standalone.json clean; vitest
tui-status-line-items.test.ts, tui-workspace-status-line.test.ts, and
status-line-picker.test.ts pass (98 tests); node
scripts/source-inventory.mjs passes with no inventory changes.
